{
  "case_id": "2006-05-595",
  "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "George J. Chanos",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Crawford v. Washington should not apply retroactively to cases on collateral review because it fails to meet the exacting standards for retroactivity established by this Court in Teague versus Lane. In addition, respondent is not entitled to relief under AEDPA. Teague held that new rules of criminal generally should not apply to cases on collateral review unless they fall within one of two narrow exceptions. The second exception, at issue here, is for those new watershed rules of criminal procedure without which the likelihood of an accurate conviction is seriously diminished, rules that alter our understanding of the bedrock procedural elements essential to a fair proceeding. Crawford is not a watershed rule of criminal procedure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We'll hear argument next in Whorton versus Bockting."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the source of the rule in Teague? Could Congress overturn the rule in Teague if it wanted to and say that nothing is retroactive or that everything is retroactive?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Irving L. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Crawford does not satisfy either of the two requirements for a retroactive watershed rule. The application of Roberts rather than Crawford did not so seriously diminish the likelihood of accurate convictions as to require the wholesale reopening of convictions that were final before Crawford was decided, with all the societial costs that entails."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is that the case in Federal courts, too?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: That's in an instruction, like Toomey versus Ohio. The judge is corrupt. It is just structural. You can't say that about Crawford, or can you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the decision that said Ring v. Arizona was not retroactive on collateral?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Forsman",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. FORSMAN: It came in under a Nevada statute which was patterned after Roberts. It came in under a Nevada statute --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Forsman",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the easiest way to explain our position on that is that what has been articulated here is that a retroactive -- a rule made retroactive by this court would be applicable to Mr. Bockting if he had not raised this issue or had been somehow procedurally defaulted along the way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is there any language in 2254(d) that could incorporate the Teague exceptions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Ms. Forsman, can I ask you a personal question? Were you a moot court finalist?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chanos",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to the interpretation of 2254(d)(1) clearly established language is inconsistent with the statement made -- statements made by this Court in Lockyer and in Williams v. Taylor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:02 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "740b212b43a48ca246dba68643f35fccc9ad0a2a3ab4895e42f6e52e293bd295",
      "evidence_id": "ev-740b212b43a4-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No one, not criminal defendants, not the judicial system, not society as a whole is benefitted by a judgment providing that a man shall tentatively go to jail today, but tomorrow and every day thereafter his continued incarceration shall be subject to fresh litigation on issues already resolved."
    },
